> Explain the difference between RAM and storage in three sentences.
RAM is volatile memory that provides fast, temporary workspace for active programs and data, losing its contents when power is turned off. Storage, such as SSDs or hard drives, is non-volatile memory used to permanently retain files, applications, and the operating system even without power. While RAM determines how many tasks a computer can handle simultaneously, storage capacity determines how much data can be saved long-term.

